DECL	{"assumptions":["asm.outside_business_district"],"binders":["x"],"id":"NRS_484B_127_3","intentions":[],"laws":["NRS-484B-127-3"],"narrowings":[{"kind":"no_atom","span":"c4","why":"'in a caravan or motorcade' is membership of an organized group of vehicles proceeding together; no atom of the surface denotes it (the record's gap ru.procession_member). The nearest atoms the record maps, rel.ahead_behind_in_lane and rel.same_direction with the motor-vehicle aggregate, hold for any two vehicles following each other in a lane, members of a group or not, as the record's own justification says: written with them, the caravan gap (22.4 m plus two 2 s headways) would bind every following motor vehicle outside a business district. The record's nearest reading (a motor vehicle ahead of x) also contradicts its own branch_1 (the lead car, with nothing ahead, bound and compliant). The same membership ('belongs to x's caravan') is unwritten in the obligation."}],"operationalizations":[{"concepts":["kin.speed","rel.ahead_behind_in_lane","rel.same_direction","rel.surface_gap"],"params":["p.entering_combination_length","p.entry_time_headway","p.same_direction_cosine"],"standard":"sufficient space ... so as to enable any other vehicle or combination of vehicles to enter and occupy such space without danger","surrogate":false}],"residues":["The duty is the same for a caravan vehicle that tows another vehicle and for one that does not: the words say so ('whether or not'); a towing vehicle and what it tows form a combination of vehicles, whose gap to the vehicle ahead is read from the combination's body through the aggregate the standard names."],"surrogate":false}
